---
// Railway is featured for its one-click setup, not required: people should know they can run Little Dipper anywhere.
---
<aside class="band" style="padding: 24px 28px">
  <div class="kicker">Your choice of host</div>
  <h3 style="font-size: 21px">Railway is featured, not required</h3>
  <p style="margin-bottom: 8px">
    We show Railway because it sets up a Little Dipper in one click. But your Little Dipper can run with any cloud provider
    that runs Docker, like Render, Fly.io or DigitalOcean, or on your own server or a small computer at home.
    It works the same everywhere, and you can move between them with a backup and your recovery kit.
  </p>
  <p class="note" style="margin: 0">
    Step-by-step guides for other providers and for self-hosting are coming soon. Comfortable with servers already?
    The <a href="https://github.com/bryanhollingshead/littledipper#readme">Little Dipper README</a> covers Docker today.
  </p>
</aside>
